Simple external interface
Whatever component is closest to the physical world — a gate controller, a mobile app backend, an attendant's terminal — should be able to park and unpark a vehicle through a single, simple call each, without needing to know about or manually coordinate spot-finding, ticket creation, and fee calculation itself.
Non-functional / stretch goal
If ticket history or spot lookups become expensive (e.g. pulled from a database) or need to be access-controlled (e.g. only admins can view another user's ticket history), that concern should be addable without changing the core lookup logic itself.

